{"author":{"id":"d4d77c46d796577aec35d160aa1e09aa095720b03e93f3ca34ad3c079140e2fb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794731232,"nonce":"1VI7JCnFOUQpgMe/QdLd+NI7pPs=","title":"Extensions cannot check the linked shader's bindings","message":"`Extension.transform` runs on each checked shader before it is inlined and linked, so it never sees the groups, bindings, entry points or native slots the shader ends up with. A framework rule such as \"group 0 holds the frame block alone\" or \"no storage buffers in shaders that must run on WebGL2\" has nowhere to run. russl's `Extension::check` takes the checked program's bindings, entry points and constants and reports diagnostics.\n\nA `check` hook on `Extension`, given the final layout (WgslLayout, LAYOUT, ENTRY_POINTS) and a position to report at, would cover it.","files":null}]}